 "notes": "1925 flats, five storeys. Sky-blue painted wood/stucco uppers, grey stucco ground storey. Two splayed bays (left of centre and right), single windows between, a railed steel fire escape in the middle, shallow cornice. Ground: small door left, grilled window, wide round-arched entry with a white surround, two windows right. Painted shields on the bay spandrels are not modelled. Rework r-eddy: brighter sky blue, navy spandrel plaques with gold medallions in both bays, gold line at the base cornice, light-blue fire escape. Tint lift (2026-10-02): paint tints lifted toward the sunlit paint (t' = 1-(1-t)k); brick tints converted to target / kit colour. Base fix (2026-10-03): cool/grey wallTint = target / painted-stucco base so the warm stucco albedo does not turn it pink. GroundBand lift (2026-10-03): groundBand tint #9a9ea6 -> #ccced2 (same rule as walls; it was missed by the first colour pass).",
